Independently distinguish complete semantic equivalence, a true one-sided
same-record extension, and material separation. Do not test every pair as if
it had to be containment. Full translations of substantive records AND complete
non-main messages may be equivalent; A/B-only strings are not semantic losses.
For an extension, name the shared subject and bind the added facts to it.
For a retained_conflict, state the two retained meanings, cite its own bilateral
context and decisive delta, and explain the actual identity/service/role/
permission/state/membership change. Buttons, navigation, language, and spacing
alone do not establish a conflict. Inspect every span; do not infer unseen roles.
Use only supplied individual span IDs in record_binding_verdict.

<semantic_diff status="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.status }}"
 contract="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.contract_version }}">
counts: {{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.span_counts }}
{% for span in payload.semantic_diff_evidence.spans %}
{% if span.kind == "SHARED" %}
[{{ span.span_id }} SHARED]
A: {{ span.a_text }}
B: {{ span.b_text }}
{% else %}
[{{ span.span_id }} {{ span.kind }}] {{ span.text }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</semantic_diff>

{% if repair_feedback %}
<repair_retry>
The previous result failed local validation. Return a fresh judgment addressing
this safe structured issue: {{ repair_feedback }}
</repair_retry>
{% endif %}
